WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.920
During Marvel Studios' panel at San Diego
Comic-Con 2019, Avengers: Infinity War and

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.410
Endgame screenwriters Christopher Markus and
Stephen McFeely revealed that Mark Ruffalo's

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.081
Bruce Banner was initially meant to merge
with his mean, green alter ego the Hulk in

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.660
Infinity War rather than in Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:18.029 --> 00:00:22.280
According to Polygon, Markus and McFeely explained
that one of the most difficult things to get

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.590
right was crafting the big character moment
where Banner finally settles his differences

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:31.599
with the Jade Giant, brings together his brain
with the Hulk's brawn, arising a smart version

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.100
of the Hulk.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:36.040
The duo wanted the character's arc to make
sense, with viewers easily understanding the

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.219
motivations behind and methods of Banner's
metamorphosis, but it turned out to be more

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.260
complicated than they initially thought.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:46.800
As Markus explained, the Infinity War team
wrote and filmed the whole transformation,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.500
saying:

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:50.640
"He achieved union with the Hulk while inside
the Hulkbuster.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:52.820
He kicked Cull Obsidian's ass."

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.880
Banner and Hulk becoming one while wearing
the Hulkbuster armor was such a hit with the

00:00:56.899 --> 00:01:01.269
Infinity War crew, they swiftly moved along
to shoot Avengers: Endgame, thinking everything

00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:04.040
was ship-shape and would be satisfying for
fans.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.180
But Markus and McFeely found flaws in their
plan to introduce Professor Hulk in Infinity

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:08.680
War.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.340
"If it works, it's gonna work, and you have
a lot of chances to find that out.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.220
And if it doesn't work, we'll circle back
around."

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.740
In their eyes, the magic of the Hulk-Banner
union subsequent butt-kicking of Black Order

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:23.420
underling Cull Obsidian faded fast, and they
realized they absolutely couldn't have that

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.020
in the film.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:24.840
Markus said:

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:25.840
"It didn't work.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.260
It was the wrong tone for the movie.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.220
A big sequence where you see the union take
away from the attention of the story."

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.370
There was a big problem, though: directors
Joe and Anthony Russo had already filmed Avengers:

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.640
Endgame, where Banner and Hulk had merged.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.700
So it was reshoots to the rescue.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.840
Markus and McFeely re-worked the Endgame script,
Banner actor Ruffalo came back to set to re-film

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.220
some sequences, and the theatrical cut of
Infinity War was permanently changed.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.880
As fans will recall, Banner does indeed join
his fellow heroes to take down Thanos and

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.270
his army of aliens across the plains of Wakanda
in Infinity War.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.940
And yes, he does wear Tony Stark's Hulkbuster
armor, because Banner had trouble bringing

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:06.820
Hulk to the surface after his initial, failed
scrap with Thanos at the beginning of the

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:07.320
movie.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.980
Following that tussle, which resulted in Loki's
death, Banner couldn't "Hulk out" no matter

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.080
how hard he tried.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.740
"How we doing? Really really good.  "

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:16.460
"Do you plan on helping out?"

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:16.960
"I'm trying!

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:17.880
He won't come out!"

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.040
Banner's arc in Avengers: Infinity War contradicted
plot points teased in the film's trailers.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.080
One featured Hulk in his full green glory
fighting side by side with Earth's Mightiest

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:28.760
Heroes.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.000
After fans saw Infinity War on the silver
screen and knew Hulk didn't show up during

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.890
that final fight, it was believed that the
clips shown in the trailers were examples

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.520
of Marvel intentionally misdirecting fans
to keep spoilers at bay.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:44.610
With Markus and McFeely's recent reveal, it
stands to reason that the clips of Hulk in

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.500
the Infinity War trailers may have come from
before the big change was made.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:54.860
Smart Hulk appears in Avengers: Endgame after
the five-year time jump from 2018 to 2023.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:58.420
The film offered a simple explanation as to
how the Banner-Hulk union happened: Banner

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:03.780
spent 18 months in the gamma lab before finding
a way to fuse his smarts with Hulk's strength.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.480
"I put the brains and the brawn together.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.340
And now look at me!"

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.670
Professor Hulk shares the information with
his Avengers pals over breakfast, where he

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.660
wolfs down pancakes and takes photos with
young fans.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.700
Markus said of the moment in Endgame,

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.920
"A scene where Hulk eats a stack of pancakes
[...] I've never seen that in a movie."

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.920
While it would have been cool to see Banner
and the Hulk collide in Infinity War, Markus

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.450
and McFeely's ultimate decision to save Professor
Hulk for Avengers: Endgame makes more sense.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:35.080
It may have undercut a moment of personal
triumph for Banner to follow it with the Snap.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:39.620
Both Endgame and Infinity War got rave reviews
for their perfect balances of action, comedy

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:40.360
and emotion.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.760
Had the screenwriters stuck to their original
plan, the reception may have been different.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:45.820
"Time travel!"

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:46.500
"Oh my God."

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:47.200
"What?"

